WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:10.490
The deal is almost done. Then the security questionnaire lands. Hundreds of questions, and every answer is a promise the company has to keep, in writing. The team has days.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:21.290
This is TrustResponse. Not one model's best guess — a team of specialized agents that drafts, challenges, and verifies every answer before it reaches the customer.

3
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.560
One drafts each response from the company's approved evidence — and cites the source behind every claim.

4
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.650
Another tears into it. Is every claim supported? Is anything overstated? Was a number invented? What's fixable gets rewritten. What the evidence can't back doesn't ship.

5
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:47.190
Then it hits a question it can't answer honestly. How often do you review who can reach production? The evidence proves reviews happen — but never how often. There's no honest number to give.

6
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:57.420
So TrustResponse doesn't invent one. It holds the answer, identifies exactly what's missing, and routes it to the team that owns the decision. It never submits a guess.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:08.960
The supported answers come back drafted, cited, and cross-checked — ready to send. The risky few are separated out, with the missing evidence and reasoning attached. A careful "needs review" beats a confident wrong answer.

8
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:16.950
The agents do the work. The person makes the call. And the deal moves forward with nothing in writing the company can't stand behind.

9
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.220
TrustResponse. Answered with evidence. Not guesswork.
